            <div xml:id="d292">

                <pb facs="0421" n="309" sameAs="frus:frus1910/pg309"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 774/769.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of
                            State to the Netherlands
                    Chargé.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1910-07-29"><hi rendition="#italic">July 29,
                        1910</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 78.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge the receipt
                    of your note of the 23d instant, by which, in accordance with instructions you
                    have received from your Government, the Government of the United States is
                    invited to be officially represented by delegates at an international conference
                    for the regulation of the commerce in opium.</p>
                <p>In reply I have the honor to say that the Government accepts with pleasure the
                    invitation of Her Majesty’s Government, and that it will at an early date
                    communicate the names of its delegates to the international conference above
                    mentioned</p>
                <p>Accept, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Huntington
                    Wilson.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
